optimization_strategy.modification_plan:
Checklist (all edits inside the existing load_inline extension; no kernel code changes):
1. EXACT ACTION — delete the two unconditional per-call permutes in `fused_resblock`:
   `auto w1c = w1.contiguous(at::MemoryFormat::ChannelsLast);`
   `auto w2c = w2.contiguous(at::MemoryFormat::ChannelsLast);`
   and replace them with `const at::Tensor& w1c = cached_cl(w1); const at::Tensor& w2c = cached_cl(w2);`. This removes 2 strided 2.36MB copy kernels (24 elementwise_kernel launches in nsys) per forward.
2. EXACT ACTION — add above `fused_resblock`:
   ```
   struct WEnt { at::Tensor t; std::vector<int64_t> sz; uint32_t ver; int dev; };
   static std::mutex g_wmu; static std::unordered_map<const void*, WEnt> g_wc;
   static const at::Tensor& cached_cl(const at::Tensor& w) {
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lk(g_wmu);
     const void* key = w.const_data_ptr();
     uint32_t ver = w.unsafeGetTensorImpl()->version_counter().current_version();
     auto it = g_wc.find(key);
     if (it != g_wc.end() && it->second.ver == ver && it->second.dev == (int)w.get_device()
         && it->second.sz == w.sizes().vec()) return it->second.t;
     if (g_wc.size() > 8) g_wc.clear();
     at::Tensor c = w.is_contiguous(at::MemoryFormat::ChannelsLast)
                    ? w : w.contiguous(at::MemoryFormat::ChannelsLast);
     auto& e = g_wc[key]; e.t = c; e.sz = w.sizes().vec(); e.ver = ver; e.dev = (int)w.get_device();
     return e.t;
   }
   ```
   Include `<mutex>`, `<unordered_map>`, `<vector>`.
3. Correctness guards: the cache key is (data_ptr, sizes, device, version-counter). Any in-place mutation of the weights bumps the version counter and forces re-conversion, so results stay bit-identical to today's path. If the tensor is non-CUDA or non-float the Python fallback is taken before the extension is called (unchanged).
4. Lifetime: cached tensors hold ~2x2.36MB of device memory; the `size() > 8` clear bounds it across the 4 benchmarked shapes (weights are shape-invariant here, so at most 2 live entries).
5. Also apply the same zero-cost fast path to the norm parameters: keep the existing `is_contiguous()` ternaries (they already avoid copies) — no change, just verify no copy kernel is emitted.
6. Do NOT touch any of the 5 CUDA kernels, their launch configs, grid/chunk derivation (the `nblk`/`chunk` re-derivation that protects the odd H*W=17161 shape must stay byte-for-byte), or the conv calls; this keeps the awkward-shape correctness property intact.
7. Optional micro-step (same mechanism, measure separately, revert on regression): cache the `partial`, `A`, `B` scratch tensors in a static map keyed by (N, C, nblk) to avoid caching-allocator lookups; only keep if the small shape (2x256x64x64) improves.
8. Validation: run all 4 shapes; assert max_atol vs reference unchanged (expect identical outputs, since only the source of an equal-valued weight buffer changed); re-run nsys and confirm `elementwise_kernel` launches drop from 24 to 0 and total launches from 180 to <=156.
9. Anti-regression check: verify with NCU that gn_apply_transpose / gn_apply_nhwc / gn_stats keep gpu__dram_throughput >= 85% and identical durations (they must be untouched); any change there indicates an accidental edit.

